meta {
  name: Delete Lab Panel
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/master-data/{{masterDataId}}/lab-panels/{{labPanelId}}
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

tests {
  test("200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
}

docs {
  🔒 **RBAC:** requires `business_admin:master_data__delete_the_panel` — enforced by `PermissionGuard` (`@RequirePermission`). A caller whose effective permissions (user override ?? branch-role override ?? role baseline) lack this get **403 `PERMISSION_DENIED`**; the `business_admin` / `administrator` roles bypass all checks, so `{{businessAccessToken}}` (an admin) still succeeds here.
  
  Soft-delete a lab panel (sets `deletedAt`) and cascade soft-delete its included
  tests in one transaction. The panel and its tests no longer appear in any list
  or get. A missing/already-deleted/foreign panel → 404 `LAB_PANEL_NOT_FOUND`.
  The freed `panelName` / `panelCode` may be reused by a new active panel.
}
